const entityStatement$1 = {"statement":"Welcome to Sanam Luang (สนามหลวง), widely recognized as the central Sanam Luang Bangkok. Located in the heart of Phra Nakhon, Bangkok, Thailand, this destination serves as a primary hub for travelers visiting the region.","hierarchyLabel":"Geographic hierarchy","hierarchy":["Sanam Luang (สนามหลวง)","Phra Nakhon","Bangkok","Thailand"],"aboutTitle":"About Sanam Luang (สนามหลวง)","aboutText":"Sanam Luang (สนามหลวง) is the historic royal square of Bangkok, Thailand — an oval public space covering roughly 74.5 rai (about 119,200 sq.m) immediately north of the Grand Palace. Host of the Royal Ploughing Ceremony and the site of major royal cremations, it works today as the city's open-air living room.","landmarksTitle":"Landmarks & Attractions Around Sanam Luang","landmarksText":"When visiting Sanam Luang (สนามหลวง), visitors can easily explore surrounding historical landmarks and points of interest, including The Grand Palace & Wat Phra Kaew and Bangkok National Museum.","historyTitle":"History & Significance of Sanam Luang (สนามหลวง)","historyText":"Originally known as Thung Phra Men (the royal cremation ground), Sanam Luang (สนามหลวง) has sat at the heart of Bangkok since the founding of the capital. It takes its present name from the grounds of the royal ceremony, and for more than two centuries it has hosted the kingdom's most important state and royal rituals."};
